TARGET: lib/node.js
REASON: The concise arrow body returns Edge#reload's value into forEach, which
discards it, and trips lint/suspicious/useIterableCallbackReturn.  Bracing the
body makes the callback return undefined explicitly; reload's return value was
never used.

---
SEARCH:
    this.edgesIn.forEach((edge) => edge.reload(true));
REPLACE:
    this.edgesIn.forEach((edge) => {
      edge.reload(true);
    });
